    "findings": [
      "Unknown or missing environment values default to development; security:check delegates to the prototype compiler check, serve emits a plan, benchmark is unimplemented, and the main guard checks only whether argv[1] ends with index.js.",
      "Compiler commands spawn the current Node executable with inherited environment and buffer complete stdout/stderr before reducing each to 80 display lines; no timeout or output-byte cap exists.",
      "Tasks run sequentially without stopping after a failed dependency. Because core-tasks can return skipped for ordinary execution, the CLI can report completed with exit zero when no operation executed. Dry-run reports are written unless --no-report, and report JSON bypasses CLI redaction. Read failures are all reported as file not found.",
      "Graph and task output paths lack a containment gate. Traversal follows stat results without realpath deduplication or cycle detection; stat failures silently omit inputs. Generated graph reads use JSON parsing plus a type assertion without schema or freshness validation, and sequential writes can leave partial output sets.",
      "The redaction replacement callback treats its second argument as an optional capture. For patterns with no capturing group JavaScript supplies the match offset, so bearer and bare-token replacements acquire a numeric prefix before SecureString(redacted). Existing tests do not assert exact replacement text for those cases.",
      "Assignment detectors run before bare-token detectors and can remove a token before the bare detector sees it. The banner counts detector names rather than token instances and does not alter process exit status. Finite regex coverage cannot justify always-safe output; uncaught errors and written reports bypass the formatter.",
      "The two Fungi assets provide only a marker and diagnostic-code constant and cite obsolete packages-galerina oracle paths. Scaffold tests invoke scripts/galerina-new.mjs and inspect generated structure/content, but the CLI command table has no new route; tests do not prove scaffold compilation or execution.",
      "Sibling dist artifacts are rebuilt through explicit package paths even though package metadata does not declare those runtime dependencies; their exact artifacts and host assumptions remain part of this package scope."
    ],
    "materialObligations": [
      "Preserve parser defaults, command dispatch, argument forwarding, exit status and main-module behavior.",
      "Preserve child-process timeout/output/error semantics and inherited environment boundaries.",
      "Preserve graph/task path, traversal, schema/freshness, partial-write and reporting behavior or explicitly narrow it before translation.",
      "Correct and differentially prove redaction replacement and report secrecy before any safe-output authority claim.",
      "Retain TypeScript as the implementation shadow; the marker-only Fungi assets are not replacements."
    ]
  },
